{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00978",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.24,
      "end_seconds": 10.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "Mr Gilligan, thanks for coming. The booking says a review of your tablets, because of the nosebleeds."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.73,
      "end_seconds": 18.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "That's right. My wife says I'm to ask. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.1,
      "end_seconds": 25.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Let's go through your tablets, one by one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.86,
      "end_seconds": 46.14,
      "duration_seconds": 18.28,
      "text": "Apixaban, 5 mg, twice a day. Bisoprolol, 5 mg, once a day. Ramipril, 5 mg, once a day. Atorvastatin, 40 mg, at night. And omeprazole, 20 mg, in the morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.82,
      "end_seconds": 53.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Good, you know them well. Do you ever miss the apixaban? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.78,
      "end_seconds": 62.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Never. It's on the kitchen table, in front of the kettle. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.26,
      "end_seconds": 71.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "That's an excellent system. Any health conditions that go with them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.85,
      "end_seconds": 79.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "The heart rhythm thing, atrial fibrillation. And high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.72,
      "end_seconds": 106.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.67,
      "text": "Let me check you. Pulse 64, blood pressure 130 over 76, temperature 36.6, oxygen 98 percent, breathing 14, weight 85 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.44,
      "end_seconds": 110.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Good numbers? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.19,
      "end_seconds": 120.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "Very good. Pulse is a nice slow one on the bisoprolol. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.21,
      "end_seconds": 124.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "That's the idea. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.12,
      "end_seconds": 131.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Any dizzy spells, Mr Gilligan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.28,
      "end_seconds": 137.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "No, no dizziness at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.32,
      "end_seconds": 153.95,
      "duration_seconds": 14.63,
      "text": "Now, here's how I think about it. The apixaban thins the blood, which protects you from a stroke from the heart rhythm, but it makes bleeding from the nose more likely. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.02,
      "end_seconds": 159.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "So it's the tablet? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.66,
      "end_seconds": 170.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.63,
      "text": "It's a contributor. But the benefit of the apixaban is large. I wouldn't want to stop it for nosebleeds alone. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.49,
      "end_seconds": 175.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "That's what the other doctor said. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.1,
      "end_seconds": 186.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "Good, we agree. The better approach is to make the nose less likely to bleed. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.49,
      "end_seconds": 191.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "How do I do that? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.83,
      "end_seconds": 202.38,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "Keep the inside of the nose moist. A small amount of petroleum jelly, just inside each nostril, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.25,
      "end_seconds": 208.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Vaseline. I have that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.48,
      "end_seconds": 217.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "A saline spray works as well. And avoid picking and forceful nose blowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.82,
      "end_seconds": 224.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "My wife says I'm a picker. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.08,
      "end_seconds": 228.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "She's observant. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.07,
      "end_seconds": 231.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "She is. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.74,
      "end_seconds": 247.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.7,
      "text": "When a nosebleed does come, sit up, lean forward, pinch the soft part of your nose for ten minutes, and breathe through your mouth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.52,
      "end_seconds": 254.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Ten minutes, by the clock. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.52,
      "end_seconds": 262.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "And don't lean back, because the blood runs down your throat. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.04,
      "end_seconds": 265.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.01,
      "end_seconds": 275.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Humidity helps too. A bowl of water by the radiator at night. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.62,
      "end_seconds": 279.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Good idea. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.78,
      "end_seconds": 288.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "If a nosebleed lasts more than twenty minutes, go straight to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.42,
      "end_seconds": 293.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Will do. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.96,
      "end_seconds": 301.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "And ring us if they're happening more than twice a week. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.67,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Understood. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
